<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fernando Pereira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fernando Pereira was a Portuguese-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> photographer working for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenpeace">Greenpeace</a>. He was killed on 10 July 1985 when agents of the French foreign intelligence service sank the Greenpeace ship Rainbow Warrior with two bombs in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auckland">Auckland</a> harbour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, before it could sail to protest against French nuclear tests at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moruroa">Moruroa</a>. He drowned when he returned below deck after the first explosion.</p></div>
